 "notes": "From eps/gagg_constraints.pdf (paper Fig. of g_agamma vs m_a). Headline MEASURED limit = COBE/FIRAS solid blue curve for B_rms^0 = 1 nG (near the Planck CMB upper bound, the leading-constraint scenario emphasized in the abstract). PIXIE (red) is a forecast/projection and NOT reported; the 0.1 and 0.01 nG blue curves are weaker benchmark B choices. Plotted y-axis is f*g_agamma where f is an O(1) geometry fudge factor (f=1/3 for isotropic angle-averaging); values reported here are the plotted f*g_agamma taken at face value (f=1). ep vector paths idx 60 (low mass) + 59 (high mass), width 1.5, color (0,0,1), solid (empty dash array). Axis calibration from tick marks: x 70.4->405.12 px = 1e-13->1e-4 eV; y 22.18 px/decade. Curve: floor ~1.2e-14 at 1e-13 eV, jump at m~1.3e-12 eV, rises through y-era to ~3-5e-12 plateau in mu-era, sharp rise near 1e-4 eV. Limit obtained from resonant gamma->a conversion sourcing CMB spectral distortions; not a dark-matter search (Omega_a<<1), so no DM density. 95% c.l. from COBE/FIRAS. eps=g_agamma*B/(1e-10 GeV^-1 nG), Eq.3c.",
